# Source preparation only

Actual author `/root/formal_oracle`. No staged source has been imported,
compiled or tested. The prior isolated bridge c27 and its 20-test result remain
immutable; they do not validate these new adapter/core/test bytes. No live core,
public source, canonical cohort, release, catalog, living report or audit was
edited. Actual remote/living completion belongs to root's receipts, not this
preparation. No production or other reviewer/producer implementation was read.

The staged files have exact intended destination paths under `staged/`:
`factory/rsm_controls.py`, `factory/pipeline.py`, `factory/exports.py`,
`factory/export_validation.py`, `oracles/independent.py`, and
`tests/rsm_core_integration_test.py`. `PROPOSED_CORE_PATCH_ATTEMPT01.diff`
encodes the same core changes against archived current base bytes. Root must
review and separately authorize installation before any live replacement.

The adapter root is explicitly `Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]` for its
intended factory location. It must not be imported from the staged directory.
Original bdbc/427/bb628 files stay at their original review paths. Exact verified
bytes load under those original filenames; no live-core fallback or translated
public IDs/version/tag grammar is introduced. Independent `option_resume`
dispatch uses official427 only; the separately authored producer route stays
root-owned. The public task remains exactly nine fields. Metadata remains
outside the task and prompt.

Direct APIs add backward-compatible optional batch arguments:
`specialized(rows,split,batch=None)`, `write_specialized(path,rows,batch=None)`,
`validate_specialized(path,rows,batch=None)`. Pipeline passes the public batch
for the RSM cohort. Once any public batch/domain/control cue selects the closed
cohort, all supplied rows remain; corruption of kind/version/track/claims or
approval flags never filters them out. An omitted batch is inferred only from
actual domain/control cues. Simultaneously erasing every cue and external batch
cannot be reconstructed from arbitrary IDs; callers must preserve the batch.

Audit adds row checks plus an error/count/source ledger from the full raw proof,
includes those errors in machine quality and preserves every earlier audit byte
using the existing history helper. Release repeats original-candidate custody
before selection/writes and accepted custody before `dest.mkdir`, including
zero and partial approvals. Validate-release repeats full custody and exact
restoration ledger checks. Direct exporters prove whole216 before choosing a
split or writing, and direct validation requires both skill split files with
typed one-per-row target coverage. Existing SFT/structured checks remain.
Legacy call sites retain their original argument form and noncohort dispatch.

Raw input loading requires original PENDING216, manifests resolved from original
claims, all six public sources, every asserted additional source, exact legacy
bytes and immutable implementation bytes. The original candidate's SHA does
not become the accepted-file SHA. Only four established review/hash fields may
change. Missing evidence is UNKNOWN/failure. Evidence and source hashes are
checked again after execution. No-follow regular-file paths reject symlinks,
escapes and nonregular inputs. New binary archives use no-follow directories
and leaves, immutable exact blobs and original-relative-path restoration.

The release source globs still preserve existing generic source behavior.
The RSM archive additionally includes bdbc/427/bb628, public six/configuration,
adapter/common/schema, target-free legacy, original raw pending JSONL, each raw
manifest and all asserted additional bytes, including non-UTF-8 bytes. Their
actual path/hash/size ledger is stored in the release manifest and joins its
source archive. No new canonical metadata field is required. Existing release
bytes are untouched; changed exporter code requires fresh code-review evidence
before any future RVM publication, not retrospective edits to earlier reviews.

Before installation, root must archive all old destination bytes and verify
the prepared base hashes plus held 222 releases, 65 references, six guards,
catalog and history boundaries under its existing custody method. Then install
